course: dictionary
lesson: 8057
title: Reinforce: making things stronger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reinforce means to make something stronger, often by adding more material or support. «Reinforced concrete has steel bars inside it so it can resist stretching as well as squashing.» The steel bars are the extra support that help the concrete hold up.
explain: The same word works for ideas and habits. Practice reinforces learning, so each time you practise, the learning gets stronger. Praise reinforces good behaviour, so the child is more likely to do the good thing again.
explain: Use context to choose the right meaning. Steel bars in concrete mean something is made stronger, while «reinforce a lesson» means make it stick in your mind. Check your meaning by swapping in "made stronger" or "made more certain" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Reinforce means to make something stronger.
fact: «Reinforced concrete» is concrete with steel bars inside it.
fact: «Reinforce the message» means to say it again or make it clearer, so people remember it.
fact: In learning, to reinforce means to repeat or reward something so it is learnt better.
fact: In history, an army can be reinforced by sending more soldiers to help it.
exercise: «Reinforced concrete has steel bars inside it so it can resist stretching as well as squashing.» What are the steel bars doing? | Painting the concrete | *Making the concrete stronger | Making it lighter to carry | Making the concrete wet
exercise: Maya says practice «reinforces learning». What does reinforces mean? | Stops the learning for a day | Makes the learning slower and harder | Makes the learning disappear | *Makes the learning stronger, so it sticks
exercise: «Praise reinforces good behaviour.» What does reinforces mean here? | *Makes the good behaviour more likely to happen again | Makes the praise quieter | Makes the good behaviour into a question | Makes the good behaviour less likely to happen again
test: «The teacher reinforced the message by saying it three times.» What does reinforced mean here? | Shouted the message out loud | Wrote the message in pencil | *Made the message clearer and easier to remember | Forgot the message completely
test: «The army was reinforced with fresh soldiers from the next town.» What does reinforced mean here? | The army went home | The army was made weaker | *More soldiers were sent to make the army stronger | The army was painted
exam: Jayden reads «The bridge was reinforced with folded paper strips.» What does reinforced mean? | Taken away completely | Made lighter and thinner | *Made stronger with extra support | Coloured in bright paint
